1. DEFINITIONS

   1.1 "Author" refers to spidychoipro, the original copyright holder
       and sole creator of this License.

   1.2 "AI System" refers to any artificial intelligence, machine learning
       model, large language model (LLM), autonomous agent, or synthetic
       computational entity capable of generating, transforming, debugging,
       or maintaining source code. This includes, but is not limited to,
       the following categories:

       (a) Web-based AI assistants:
           - OpenAI ChatGPT (chat.openai.com)
           - Google Gemini (gemini.google.com)
           - Anthropic Claude Web (claude.ai)
           - Microsoft Copilot (copilot.microsoft.com)
           - Perplexity AI (perplexity.ai)

       (b) AI-powered coding agents and IDEs:
           - Anthropic Claude Code (CLI)
           - OpenAI Codex CLI (codex)
           - OpenCode (opencode.ai)
           - Agy
           - Cursor (cursor.com)
           - Windsurf (windsurf.com)
           - Cline (VS Code extension)
           - Aider (aider.chat)
           - GitHub Copilot Agent
           - Amazon Q Developer
           - JetBrains AI Assistant

       (c) Self-hosted or API-based models:
           - OpenAI GPT series (GPT-4, GPT-4o, o1, o3, etc.)
           - Anthropic Claude series (Claude 3.5, Claude 4, etc.)
           - Google Gemini series (Gemini 2.0, Gemini Ultra, etc.)
           - Meta Llama series
           - Mistral AI models
           - DeepSeek series
           - Any locally deployed large language model capable of code
             generation

       (d) Any future artificial intelligence system, regardless of
           naming, architecture, or vendor, that possesses the capability
           to generate, modify, or debug source code.

   1.3 "Human User" refers to any natural person or legal entity that
       interacts with, uses, modifies, or distributes the Software.

   1.4 "Software" refers to the source code, binary executables, scripts,
       configuration files, documentation, build artifacts, and all
       related materials governed under this License.

   1.5 "AI-Generated Modification" refers to any code change, addition,
       deletion, refactoring, optimization, or transformation produced
       by an AI System operating under the direction of a Human User.

   1.6 "Direct Code Modification" means any manual insertion, deletion,
       replacement, or alteration of source code executed directly by a
       Human User via physical keyboard, text editor, IDE, binary patch,
       or command-line interface without passing through an AI System.

   1.7 "Natural Language Directive" means any non-code, natural language
       instruction, request, context specification, or high-level
       functional specification transmitted by a Human User to an AI
       System for the purpose of guiding code generation or modification.

   1.8 "Redistribution" means copying, sublicensing, or transmitting the
       Software to third parties, whether for commercial or non-commercial
       purposes.

   1.9 "Derivative Work" means any work based upon, derived from, or
       incorporating the Software, including translations, adaptations,
       and AI-Generated Modifications.

